.TH EXTENSIONS 3ggl "11 August 1997" "GGL/IGP ETHZ" "GGL Common Lib"
.SH NAME
remove_extension, get_extension \- filename extension operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <common/inout.h>

.RB "char *" remove_extension
.RI "(char *" filename ");"

.RB "char *" get_extension
.RI "(const char *" filename ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The function 
.B remove_extension()
will truncate the string
.I filename
by replacing the last dot in the string by a zero character.
The string passed to this function will be modified!

.B get_extension()
returns a pointer to a newly allocated string containing the
extension including the leading dot. The string
.I filename
that it is passed as an argument will not be altered!
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
.B remove_extension()
will always return the pointer to
.IR filename ,
no matter whether there was an extension to be remove or not.

.B get_extension()
returns a pointer to a newly allocated string containing the
extension including the leading dot.
When no extension was present in
.IR filename ,
this function will return a
.B NULL
pointer.
.SH ERRORS
When no extension was present in
.IR filename ,
.B get_extension()
will return a
.B NULL
pointer.
.B remove_extension()
does not know about any error condition.
.SH CAVEATS
You have to compile your program using
.I -lcommon
as a compiler flag to properly link
your function to the library.
